# {{ .App.Name }}

Generated by `opencli` for the Rust target.

## Build

```bash
cargo build
```

## Version

Generated Rust CLIs use the package version `{{ rustAppVersion .App }}` from `Cargo.toml` for `--version`. Set this value with `opencli generate --app-version` or `opencli.yaml app.version`.

```bash
target/release/{{ .App.Name }} --version
```

## Run

{{- if appHasAnyMCP .App }}
Set the generated MCP endpoint when needed:

```bash
export OPENCLI_BASE_URL='http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp'
```
{{- else }}
Set the target API base URL:

```bash
export OPENCLI_BASE_URL='http://127.0.0.1:8000'
```
{{- end }}

```bash
cargo run -- --help
```

## Runtime Configuration

The launcher reads `config/runtime.yaml` by default. Set `OPENCLI_CONFIG` to select another YAML file. `OPENCLI_BASE_URL` and the applicable credential environment variable are plaintext per-run overrides and take priority over the sealed value in the file.

{{- if appUsesToken .App }}
## Auth

Mode: `token`

Set the generated token before running commands that require authentication:

```bash
export OPENCLI_AUTH_TOKEN='your-token'
```

The CLI injects `Authorization: Bearer <token>` when no explicit `Authorization` header is provided.
{{- else if appUsesAPIKey .App }}
## Auth

Mode: `api_key`

`config/runtime.yaml` declares the API-key header. Set `OPENCLI_API_KEY` only when a plaintext per-run override is needed. An explicit matching `--header` value has highest priority.
{{- else if appUsesAKSK .App }}
## Auth

Mode: `ak_sk`

This CLI signs HTTP requests internally. Set credentials before running commands:

```bash
export OPENCLI_AK='your-access-key'
export OPENCLI_SK='your-secret-key'
```

Requests include `appKey`, `sign`, `timestamp`, and `nonce` headers. Signer profile: `{{ appSignerProfile .App }}`.

The `supplier_edi` profile uses the supplier `sha512Hex` canonical string: `method`, `/v2...` path, `appKey`, `appSecret`, `timestamp`, `nonce`, and compact `jsonBody`.
{{- else if appUsesOAuth2 .App }}
## Auth

{{- if and .RuntimeBundle (eq .RuntimeBundle.OAuth2GrantType "authorization_code") }}
Mode: `oauth2` (`authorization_code`)

Run `target/release/{{ .App.Name }} login` to authenticate in the IAM browser flow. The CLI sends the returned authorization code to the configured business `token_url`, stores the business access token locally, and injects `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>` for protected operations. Run `target/release/{{ .App.Name }} logout` to delete the local session.
{{- else }}
Mode: `oauth2` (`client_credentials`)

The CLI obtains an access token from the configured OAuth token endpoint and injects `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>` for protected operations. The public `client_id` and sealed client secret are stored in `config/runtime.yaml`. Set `OPENCLI_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET` only for a plaintext per-run override.
{{- end }}
{{- else }}
## Auth

Mode: `none`

This CLI does not inject authentication headers. Use `-H` / `--header` only when an endpoint needs non-auth routing or internal gateway headers.
{{- end }}

## Header Input

HTTP commands accept repeatable `-H` / `--header` flags:

```bash
cargo run -- <group> <command> -H "ACCESS-STATUS=inner"
cargo run -- <group> <command> --header "ACCESS-STATUS=inner"
```

## Generated Skills

Each generated project includes standardized command-group skill packages{{ if gt (len .App.Groups) 1 }} plus a router skill for agent loaders{{ end }}:

```bash
cargo run -- skills list
cargo run -- skills read <skill>
cargo run -- skills --skills-dir /path/to/skills read <skill>
```

```text
skills/
{{ if gt (len .App.Groups) 1 }}
├── SKILL.md
├── README.md
{{ else }}
├── README.md
{{ end }}
└── <group>/
    ├── SKILL.md
    ├── README.md
    ├── assets/
    │   └── demo-request.json
    ├── references/
    │   ├── command-routing.md
    │   ├── commands.md
    │   ├── workflows.md
    │   └── production-checklist.md
    └── generation-report.md
```

`--data` accepts inline JSON, `@file`, `-` for stdin, and `@@...` for a literal `@`. Commands with binary upload fields expose `--file path` or `--file field=path`; multipart text fields belong in `--data`. Do not use `--data -` and `--file -` together.

Generated skills are API scaffolds.{{ if gt (len .App.Groups) 1 }} Root `skills/SKILL.md` is a router for agent loaders;{{ end }} per-group `SKILL.md` files hold the command guidance. `assets/demo-request.json` is valid placeholder JSON and can be used immediately with `--data @assets/demo-request.json`; `generation-report.md` lists source documentation gaps. Before production, fill the MANUAL sections with business intent, routing rules, workflows, safety constraints, and validation evidence.

`skills list` and `skills read` read the generated `skills/` folder from disk so manual business edits are visible to agents. Run them from the generated project root, or pass `--skills-dir /path/to/skills` when the CLI binary is installed elsewhere.
